   "caption": "There\u2019s a seventeen thousand dollar grant for painters just starting out. No CV, no deadline, no fee, and it\u2019s open worldwide.\n\nIt\u2019s the Elizabeth Greenshields Foundation. Yesterday I mentioned a fund paying painters up to fifty thousand, and I was honest that it wants around ten years of exhibitions behind you. This is the other one. This one is built for the beginning.\n\nCAD 17,000 for a first grant. 20,000 if they fund you again. No application fee. And no deadline at all, they take applications right through the year from anywhere in the world. Last year they gave out close to 1.6 million between 93 artists.\n\nTwo honest catches. It has to be representational work: painting, drawing, sculpture, printmaking. If you work abstract, this one isn\u2019t yours. And you have to print, sign and post the application. An actual envelope, in 2026.\n\nIf that rules you out, here\u2019s a second one. The Awesome Foundation gives away 1,000 dollars every single month, no strings, no fee, and the eligibility rule is essentially: if you can fill in the form, you can apply. No CV. Chapters across the US, UK, Australia and Canada. Pick the one nearest you.\n\nYesterday\u2019s fund had a ten year bar on it. This one was built for people at the start. Not everything is gated. You\u2019ve just never been shown the ungated ones.\n\nSend this to a painter who thinks it\u2019s too early for them.\n@elizabethgreenshieldsfdn \n@awesomefound \n#ArtistGrants #ArtFunding #EmergingArtist #PainterLife #CreativeFlair",
