   "creator_full": "Shakib Hammad",
   "caption": "Melvin Conway sent this to Harvard Business Review in 1967 and they rejected it for not proving its thesis. Datamation ran it a year later. The claim: any organisation that designs a system produces a design that copies that organisation\u2019s own communication structure. Four teams building a compiler ship a compiler with four parts.\nThe elaboration the video does not make: engineers now use this deliberately and call it the reverse Conway manoeuvre. Decide the architecture you want first, then arrange the teams to match, because the mirroring happens either way and the only real choice is whether it happens on purpose.\nYour customers are holding a physical copy of your org chart, and they experience it as friction. Which handoff in your product is really two teams that barely speak?\n\nWhat to do about it, written out properly: shakibhammad.com/library/conway\n\nAnd if you want the version of this that is about you rather than your company, the reading on the site names what you actually do in six situations. Free, ten minutes, nothing sold at the end.\n\n#startupfounder #processdesign #leadership #teambuilding #decisionmaking",
